<title>BAHRAIN: ISLAMIC DEVELOPMENT BANK LENDS AZERBAIJAN $13 MLN.</title>
<headline>ISLAMIC DEVELOPMENT BANK LENDS AZERBAIJAN $13 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Islamic Development Bank (IDB) has lent Azerbaijan $13 million to finance a road project, an IDB statement said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The loan would be repaid in 20 years with a five-year grace period, the statement said. The deal raised total IDB financing provided to Azerbaijan to $30 million, it added.</p>
<p>The Jeddah-based bank, set up in 1975, helps finance and promote trade between Moslem states.</p>
</text>
